docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:32:## 2. Summary verdict
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:34:**This revision resolves the substantive reporting problems from the previous round, and the new paired analysis is correct and useful.** It now shows more clearly that R3’s measured relative performance deteriorates within the sampled markets, while keeping that finding separate from an ordering that would hold across other markets. The reference-reselection diagnostic, Run B selection, low-rate comparisons, W1 scope, and theory qualification are corrected. I found no new numerical error in the revised results. One interval-scope sentence still needs correction, partly because my own proposed wording last round was too broad. There are also small abstract, response-document, and test-path fixes. My scores remain **WEIS 2027: 3/5, upper borderline; AAMAS main track: 2/5; ACM EC: 1/5**. The paper’s reporting is stronger, but its scientific reach still rests on the same markets, comparator coverage, and incomplete churn searches. Those disclosed limits constrain the contribution; they do not make the present narrow conclusions false.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:36:## 3. Follow-through on round-5 problems 1–11
