docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:177:### D. Mechanism
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:181:It covers both relevant selected behaviours. Some attackers remain old and receive little attention after their priority window. Others replace, but are rarely uniquely newest among identities holding jobs. The new statistic adds direct evidence for the latter description.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:191:Source: `records/churn/p0.05/diagnostics.json`, `shares.focal_newest_by_first_offer_assigned`, reproduced in **C**, `review_r5.focal_newest_by_market["0.05"]`.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:195:One interpretive distinction should remain clear: being uniquely newest among all job-holding identities is stronger than being uniquely newest among established identities. The new frequency is useful descriptive evidence, but it is not the exact frequency with which every condition of the residual-targeting lemma holds. The paper does not currently make that stronger inference.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext2.md:201:No new causal claim needs to be removed. The missing no-churn allocation baseline would improve the description, but it is not needed to validate the allocation measurements at nonzero rates or the new paired performance analysis.
