docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:56:## 4. The churn section
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:58:### (a) Plan fidelity
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:60:**The implementation and scoring agree with the written estimand and expectations. The claimed timing is internally consistent, but not independently proved by this archive.**
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:62:The original plan discloses the timing peek before expectations 1–4. The amendment discloses that the endpoint results were known before expectations 5–8 were written. It compares each search version with its own corresponding no-churn values, uses equal market weights, and keeps the reference candidate fixed while evaluating it under churn.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:64:The ledger places amendment commit `2604ce6` before the new runs at `e1c925a`; the new records identify the latter commit in their provenance. This supports the stated sequence. The archive lacks the Git object history or independent timestamp evidence needed to verify that sequence independently. Sources: `churn-plan-amendment-1.md`, §§1–3; `operations-ledger.md`, “Churn amendment 1”; new-rate record provenance.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:66:The amendment’s expectations reproduce as follows:
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:75:Source: reproduced `M.expectations["5"…"8"]`. Expectations 1–4 also reproduce as met from `C.expectations`.
docs/revision/roster/astra-pro-paper-d10-ext.md:77:The paper is right to say that these expectations carried limited risk after the earlier observations. Their success is not an independent validation of the mechanism.
